ok   config/app.rb explains DATABASE_URL
ok   .env.example names the development database
ok   the Dockerfile's run example passes DATABASE_URL; storage/ keeps the uploads
ok   config/deploy.yml takes DATABASE_URL as a secret and says what one process guarantees
skip config/deploy.yml (MySQL: the worker role stays commented; jobs in several processes are not guaranteed until step 2, see the configuration guide, "MySQL")
insert config/deploy.yml (the worker role, uncommented)
ok   generate job and generate authentication leave a MySQL app's worker role commented
ok   AGENTS.md says the application is on MySQL and requires cybertrain/mysql
ok   .kamal/secrets reads DATABASE_URL from the environment
ok   the CI workflow runs the tests against a MySQL service
ok   every other file is SQLite's
identical bin/shop.rb (require "cybertrain/mysql" loads cybertrain/jobs)
identical bin/db.rb (require "cybertrain/mysql" loads cybertrain/jobs)
ok   a subsystem's require is not added: cybertrain/mysql loads them all
